# Forge's route search orders the quests of this guide and its guide writer writes the steps.
# Fixes go into data/route-fixes.json, data/guide-fixes.json or forever-db/corrections, never
# into this file.
# Left out: A Little Luck (6606), A Strange One (6605).
# Flow (2026-11-20): this guide starts where 50-60/02 ends, in the Timbermaw tunnel: Salfa -> Donova's accepts ->
# Everlook (yetis, chimaeras) -> back west: Raging Owlbeasts and the Frostfire camps (their Den Watchers are 55-56:
# done after Everlook's errands, at about 54 by the level model, and the tip sends you at the 55s) -> Donova -> Everlook -> fly to Splintertree Post -> Felwood's southern
# hand-ins on one ride north (Ror, the Emerald Sanctuary, Winna's flasket at the Jadefire moonwell, Bloodvenom Post,
# Winna's kitten) -> fly to Camp Mojache (Talo, the Videre Elixir) -> Shadowprey Village -> Thunder Bluff. Felwood's
# back-south ride from Timbermaw Hold and the second ride north into the tunnel are gone; the Orgrimmar stop and
# its cloth donations open 50-60/04 after Ratchet and the Crossroads. The older notes below describe the export.

step Into Winterspring
  zone Winterspring
  goto 28.0,34.6 "Into Winterspring"

step Salfa
  tip Salfa stands right at the Winterspring exit of Timbermaw Hold's tunnel, where you come out.
  turnin 8465

step Donova Snowden
  tip Ride south from the tunnel: Donova camps among the steaming pools of Frostfire Hot Springs, in the west of the valley.
  turnin 3908 -- Linken's Training Sword
  accept 3909
  accept 5082
  turnin 980                          -- The New Springs, from Krakle in Un'Goro
  note The Videre Elixir comes from Gregan Brewspewer in Feralas, later in this guide. Donova's next errand, Strange Sources, is at the mouth of Darkwhisper Gorge among level 59-60 elites: it waits for the last guide's Winterspring loop.

step Winterspring
  zone Winterspring
  tip Ride east along the road past Lake Kel'Theril to Everlook first: its yeti and chimaera errands bring you about a quarter of a level, which the Frostfire furbolg camps want; Donova's camps come on the ride back west.
  goto 60.7,38.2 "Everlook"
# Built from the playthrough simulator's consensus route (Horde, visits
# 74-79) and machine-checked with lint; not play-tested on Forever yet.
#
# 0.3.7 (Horde 40-60 flow pass): west to east. Salfa -> Donova and the
# Frostfire Hot Springs camps -> Raging Owlbeasts on the road east ->
# Everlook (Umi's yetis, Felnok's chimaeras) -> Winterfall Village -> fly.
# Meggi's Trouble in Winterspring! (6603), a pointer to Donova, is left out.
# The older notes below describe the export's order.
#
# Flow: Everlook (Gregor, Felnok, Harlo, Umi, Meggi) -> Ice Thistle yetis ->
# Chillwind chimaeras -> Everlook -> ride west (Raging Owlbeasts) -> Donova
# Snowden -> Salfa -> Frostfire Winterfall camps -> Salfa -> Donova ->
# Darkwhisper Gorge -> Winterfall Village -> Donova -> Salfa (beads) ->
# hearth to Everlook -> grind to 55 -> Mau'ari -> fly to Camp Mojache
# (Videre Elixir, Talo) -> Thunder Bluff (Morrowgrain, Hamuul, Nara, cloth
# donations, Druid and Paladin training) -> Orgrimmar (bind, cloth
# donations), where the next guide
# starts.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Umi's and Meggi's quests (3783, 6603) are taken on arrival in Everlook
#   and the yetis done straight away, since their hills are next to town;
#   the export takes them after its first hearth. That first hearth (54.7)
#   becomes a ride: Darkwhisper Gorge and Winterfall Village lie east of
#   Donova anyway.
# - The Desolace stop (visit 77) is dropped: its only "objectives" are the
#   Thunder Bluff cloth donations (7820-7822), which are just cloth carried in
#   your bags. The same goes for the Mageweave donations the export
#   "completes" in Azshara (7831, 7835): every Thunder Bluff and Orgrimmar
#   donation is handed in on the stop that takes it (final review, 0.3.5),
#   so the Azshara guide has no second Orgrimmar stop for them.
# - Binds immediately replaced are dropped (Camp Mojache, Thunder Bluff);
#   the Orgrimmar bind is kept for the hearth at the end. No bind at
#   Everlook (0.4.0): no step hearths back there. The trip to Camp Mojache is
#   now a flight from Bloodvenom Post at the end of Felwood's ride north.
# - Dropped: In Defense of Frostwolf (7241, a battleground quest); Return to
#   Tinkee (4810: Burning Steppes, never on the later route) and Duke
#   Hydraxis' Poisoned Water and Stormers and Rumblers (6804, 6805: the
#   later guides no longer hand them in, the Duke's chain runs on past 60).
#   A Crew Under Fire (3382): six naga waves at 57 on Azshara's Southridge
#   Beach, with elite giants close by, for 600 XP, and a flight, a long ride
#   and a hearth.
#   Winterfall Activity (6241): no longer in the game; 8464, which the
#   route takes, replaced it.
# - Winterfall Firewater (5083) and Falling to Corruption (5084) are taken
#   (0.3.7): the Empty Firewater Flask drops from one Winterfall kill in ten
#   (Forever's loot data and the server's loot table agree), and the hot
#   springs alone take 24 of them. Optional: Winterfall Ritual Totem
#   (8471): the totem drops at 2-4%, and Kernda in Timbermaw Hold speaks
#   only to characters at Neutral, which the route does not reach.
# - Not taken: Guarding Secrets (4882, 4883, to Nara Wildmane here). The
#   Blue-feathered Necklace that starts it drops from Winterspring's
#   Moontouched and Berserk Owlbeasts only after Wild Guardians (4741) is
#   done: 4741 is taken from Trull on this guide's Bloodvenom stop and done on
#   the last guide's Winterspring loop, which takes Guarding Secrets (4882) too.
#
# Left open for later guides: The Everlook Report (6029) and Duke Nicholas
# Zverenhoff (6030, Plaguelands), A Strange One (6605), Runecloth (6031: keep
# 30 Runecloth for Meilosh), Wild Guardians' next part (4741, Trull), Falling
# to Corruption (5084) and Winterfall Ritual Totem (8471, both in Felwood),
# The Videre Elixir (3909, back to Donova), Are We There, Yeti? (5163: the
# goblins in Tanaris and Un'Goro), Rabine Saturna (1123, Moonglade) and the
# cloth donations.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Everlook

step Everlook
  tip Everlook is the goblin town on the east side of the valley, past the owlbeast hills.
  getfp "Everlook"
  note Gregor's quests lead to other zones: keep them.
  accept 3783                         -- Umi Rumplesnicker
  accept 6029                         -- Gregor Greystone, inside
  accept 6030
  turnin 4808                         -- Felnok Steelspring
  accept 4809

step Ice Thistle yetis
  tip The yeti hills start just south-east of Everlook. Every yeti drops fur. Careful: the Ice Thistle Yetis are 55-56: take the 55s one at a time, and leave the Matriarchs and Patriarchs (56-58), whose horns come on a later visit.
  collect 12366 quest 3783

step Chillwind chimaeras
  tip The chimaeras roam the snowfields south and west of Everlook. Careful: Chillwind Chimaeras are 55-57: take only the 55s, and the Fledgling Chillwinds (53-55) by Lake Kel'Theril, which carry the horns too. Stay clear of Mazthoril's cave: its blue dragonkin are elite.
  collect 12444 quest 4809

step Everlook
  turnin 3783                         -- Umi Rumplesnicker
  accept 977                          -- Umi: keep it, the Pristine Yeti Horns come on the Eastern Plaguelands guide's Everlook stop at about 56
  turnin 4809                         -- Felnok Steelspring
  note The Matriarchs and Patriarchs that carry Umi's horns are 56-58: leave them for that later stop.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Frostfire Hot Springs

step Raging Owlbeasts
  tip Ride back west: Raging Owlbeasts roam the hills north of Lake Kel'Theril, by the road between Everlook and Frostfire Hot Springs. Careful: the biggest are level 56: pull them one at a time.
  kill 7451 quest 4521.1

step Frostfire Hot Springs: kill these as you meet them
  zone Winterspring
  tip Pathfinders, Den Watchers and Totemics share the furbolg camps around the hot springs; Ragged Owlbeasts roam the slopes between them. Kill Totemics first. Save every Runecloth you loot for Meilosh.
  tip Careful: the Den Watchers are 55-56: pull the 55s, one at a time, and keep clear of the camps' totems.
  kill 7442 quest 5082.1
  kill 7441 quest 5082.3
  kill 7440 quest 5082.2
  kill 7450 quest 4521.2
  collect 12771                       -- Empty Firewater Flask: about one Winterfall furbolg in ten carries one; keep killing them until it drops
  accept 5083
  collect 20742 optional              -- Winterfall Ritual Totem, a rare drop from the Winterfall furbolgs
  accept 8471 optional

step Donova Snowden
  turnin 5082
  turnin 5083
  accept 5084
  note Falling to Corruption is turned in at the Deadwood Cauldron in Felwood, on a later trip.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Southern Felwood, south to north

step Fly to Splintertree Post
  zone Winterspring
  tip Felwood's southern hand-ins are next: ride back east to Everlook's flight master, fly to Splintertree Post (by way of Valormok) and ride north into Felwood, so the forest is ridden once, south to north.
  goto 60.5,36.3 "Everlook flight master"
  fly "Splintertree Post"
  zone Ashenvale

step Overlord Ror
  zone Felwood
  tip Ride north-west along the road into Felwood. Ror stands at the far south end of Deadwood Village, just inside the border.
  collect 15879 quest 6162 @48.2,94.3

step Taronn Redfeather
  when complete 5156
  tip North to the druids' camp.
  turnin 5156                         -- Taronn Redfeather

